\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs24\lang9\par
Exploratory Data Analysis for Machine Learning\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qc\b\fs36 Week 1.\par
A brief history of AI and its applications\par
Learning Objectives\b0\fs24\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1 Artificial Intelligence is not new, but it is new in a sense that it is easier than ever to get started using Machine Learning in business settings. In this module, we will go over a quick introduction to AI and Machine Learning and we will visit a brief history of the modern AI. We will also explore some of the current applications of AI and Machine Learning for you, to think about how you want to leverage them in your day to day business practice or personal projects.\par
Learning Objectives\par
Become familiar with common Machine Learning vocabulary and the Machine Learning Workflow\par
Become familiar with Modern AI applications, including Computer Vision and Natural Language Processing\par
Become familiar with the chronology of Artificial Intelligence, including AI booms and AI winters\par
Become familiar with the definitions of Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and Deep Learning\par
\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1\qc\b\fs52 Review\b0\fs24\par

\pard\sa200\sl240\slmult1 Introduction to Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning\par
Artificial Intelligence is a branch of computer science dealing with the simulation of intelligent behavior in computers. Machines mimic cognitive functions such as learning and problem solving. \par
\par
Machine learning is the study of programs that are not explicitly programmed, but instead these algorithms learn patterns from data. \par
\par
Deep learning is a subset of machine learning in which multilayered neural networks learn from vast amounts of data.   \par
\par
\b\fs32 History of AI \par
\b0\fs24 AI has experienced cycles of AI winters and AI booms. \par
\par
AI solutions include speech recognition, computer vision, assisted medical diagnosis, robotics, and others.   \par
\par
\b\fs32 Modern AI \par
\b0\fs24 Factors that have contributed to the current state of Machine Learning are: bigger data sets, faster computers, open-source packages, and a wide range of neural network architectures.   \par
\par
