JSON files are a standard way to store data across platforms. Their structure is similar to Python dictionaries.\par
\par
NoSQL databases are not relational and vary more in structure. Most NoSQL databases store data in JSON format.\par
\par
\b\fs48 Data Cleaning\par
\b0\fs36 Data Cleaning is important because messy data will lead to unreliable outcomes.Some common issues that make data messy are: duplicate or unnecessary data, inconsistent data and typos, missing data, outliers, and data source issues.\par
\par
You can identify duplicate or unnecessary dataCommon policies to deal with missing data are:remove a row with missing columns, impute the missing data, and mask the data by creating a category for missing values.\par
\par
Common methods to find outliers are: through plots, statistics, or residuals.\par
\par
Common policies to deal with outliers are: remove outliers, impute them, use a variable transformation, or use a model that is resistant to outliers.\par
\par
